{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>וילד</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other כי איש הרגתי לפצעי וילד לחבורתי. For if we leave Benjamin here, it is as though 'I have slain a man,' that is, Jacob, 'for my wound,' and 'a young child' for 'my bruise,' that is, Benjamin, for it is impossible for them to live one without the other." "<b> וילד זקנים</b> defective — for he transmitted to him everything he learned from the elders, that is, Shem and Eber. ויותר two times in the Masorah: here and the other ויותר יעקב לבדו. Just as there it refers to war, as written 'and a man wrestled with him,' so too here he prepared himself for war."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:23.232692843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}